WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.892 --> 00:00:14.935
The day after Tom and Huck's adventure in the tavern, Becky reminded everyone that she was having a

2
00:00:14.975 --> 00:00:17.796
picnic. This interrupted Tom's thoughts.

3
00:00:18.677 --> 00:00:21.857
He stopped dreaming of Injun Joe, and he stopped dreaming of gold.

4
00:00:22.658 --> 00:00:25.278
The only thing he could think about was Becky and the picnic.

5
00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:27.959
That night Tom couldn't sleep.

6
00:00:28.919 --> 00:00:30.620
He stayed up, waiting for Huck to call.

7
00:00:32.716 --> 00:00:36.718
But Huck didn't call, so the next morning a sleepy Tom joined the rest of the children at

8
00:00:36.759 --> 00:00:37.579
the ferry landing.

9
00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:43.503
As they were getting ready to board the ferry, Tom overheard Becky's mother tell her, "You'll be getting

10
00:00:43.543 --> 00:00:44.163
back late.

11
00:00:45.344 --> 00:00:47.985
Why don't you stay with the Harpers tonight, near the landing."

12
00:00:49.646 --> 00:00:51.667
When Tom heard this, he hatched a plan.

13
00:00:51.687 --> 00:00:57.151
"Becky," he said, "let's spend the night at Widow Douglas' house instead.

14
00:00:58.011 --> 00:00:59.112
She'll have ice cream."

15
00:00:59.852 --> 00:01:03.573
Becky was about to say no when Tom reminded her that her mother would never know.

16
00:01:04.574 --> 00:01:05.314
So she agreed.

17
00:01:06.034 --> 00:01:10.255
The ferry dropped the picnickers off at a spot about three miles from town.

18
00:01:12.196 --> 00:01:17.158
After they had eaten and played some games, somebody yelled, "Who's ready for the cave?"

19
00:01:18.178 --> 00:01:20.459
Everyone shouted, "Yay!"

20
00:01:20.479 --> 00:01:23.680
So candles were quickly provided, and the children entered the cave.

21
00:01:24.588 --> 00:01:29.389
The cave was a confusing maze of twisting and turning tunnels, but most of the boys knew their

22
00:01:29.429 --> 00:01:30.390
way around a lot of it.

23
00:01:31.330 --> 00:01:34.211
After a while the boys and girls returned to the cave entrance.

24
00:01:35.431 --> 00:01:36.912
Soon the ferry blew its whistle.

25
00:01:37.752 --> 00:01:39.632
Night was falling, and it was time to go.

26
00:01:40.493 --> 00:01:44.534
The picnickers boarded the boat and amused themselves with tales of their adventures.

27
00:01:45.434 --> 00:01:47.875
No one noticed that Tom and Becky were missing.

28
00:01:50.535 --> 00:01:52.276
Meanwhile Huck was watching the tavern.

29
00:01:53.164 --> 00:01:57.106
Huck was hiding deep in the shadows when he saw two men leave by the alley door.

30
00:01:58.406 --> 00:02:02.228
To Huck's surprise, one of the men seemed to be carrying a box under his arm.

31
00:02:02.928 --> 00:02:07.170
Huck was determined not to let the treasure escape him twice, so he followed the men.

32
00:02:10.471 --> 00:02:13.492
They headed toward the ferry landing, and then a little out of town.

33
00:02:14.793 --> 00:02:16.794
They stopped near the Widow Douglas' house.

34
00:02:16.814 --> 00:02:20.495
"There are lights on," growled Injun Joe.

35
00:02:20.515 --> 00:02:22.156
"She must have company."

36
00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:25.382
"Maybe we shouldn't do this," said the second man.

37
00:02:25.402 --> 00:02:27.903
"No way," said Injun Joe.

38
00:02:27.923 --> 00:02:29.644
"I want revenge.

39
00:02:30.565 --> 00:02:35.227
Her husband horsewhipped me, but he died before I could—" "Are you going to kill her?"

40
00:02:35.608 --> 00:02:36.668
interrupted the other man.

41
00:02:36.688 --> 00:02:38.509
"I won't do any killing."

42
00:02:38.529 --> 00:02:41.251
"Kill? Who said kill?"

43
00:02:41.611 --> 00:02:42.572
answered Injun Joe.

44
00:02:43.332 --> 00:02:44.232
Huck had heard enough.

45
00:02:44.913 --> 00:02:46.574
He turned and slowly moved away.

46
00:02:47.334 --> 00:02:49.676
Once he was sure that he couldn't be heard or seen, he ran.

47
00:02:51.872 --> 00:02:53.813
Huck stopped at the first house he came to.

48
00:02:54.633 --> 00:02:57.174
It was the Welshman's house, and he banged on the door.

49
00:02:57.914 --> 00:03:02.435
As soon as the Welshman opened the door, Huck told him that Widow Douglas might be in danger.

50
00:03:03.336 --> 00:03:06.496
The Welshman and his sons grabbed their guns and ran into the night.

51
00:03:07.457 --> 00:03:09.617
Huck returned at dawn to learn what had happened.

52
00:03:09.637 --> 00:03:14.339
"Sit down, boy," said the Welshman.

53
00:03:14.359 --> 00:03:17.720
"First we'll have breakfast, and then we'll trade stories."

54
00:03:18.948 --> 00:03:24.030
After breakfast Huck learned that Injun Joe and his partner had gotten away, but that the box contained

55
00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:25.290
only thieves' tools.

56
00:03:26.130 --> 00:03:28.271
Huck told the Welshman almost everything he knew.

57
00:03:28.931 --> 00:03:32.612
The Welshman was shocked that he and his boys had almost captured Injun Joe.

58
00:03:34.273 --> 00:03:38.094
All through the morning Huck stayed out of sight because he didn't want anyone to know that he

59
00:03:38.134 --> 00:03:38.774
was involved.

60
00:03:39.594 --> 00:03:43.455
The Welshman had a lot of visitors who wanted to hear the tale, and he told them.

61
00:03:44.335 --> 00:03:49.187
But he never mentioned Huck's name; instead he described a mystery man who had warned him of the

62
00:03:49.227 --> 00:03:54.851
crime. Soon the town was as curious about the mystery man as they were about the crime.

63
00:03:55.912 --> 00:03:58.034
But the Welshman wouldn't reveal Huck's identity.

64
00:03:59.235 --> 00:04:03.959
Although there was no Sunday school during summer vacation, the whole town gathered at the church.

65
00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:08.963
People wanted to hear more news about the thieves and the mystery man.

66
00:04:10.344 --> 00:04:14.928
Before long a new mystery appeared: where were Becky Thatcher and Tom Sawyer?

67
00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:16.340
No one knew.

68
00:04:17.321 --> 00:04:20.622
Judge Thatcher organized a search party, and the group went to the cave.

69
00:04:21.382 --> 00:04:25.584
They looked for Becky and Tom for three straight days, but were unable to find them.

70
00:04:26.404 --> 00:04:30.546
The only thing they found was Tom and Becky's names written on the wall of the cave.

71
00:04:32.787 --> 00:04:37.429
While Huck was following the thieves and most of the town was sleeping, Tom and Becky had become

72
00:04:37.489 --> 00:04:38.329
lost in the cave.

73
00:04:39.390 --> 00:04:44.512
Tom was an experienced explorer, but while he was with Becky, he had forgotten to mark their path.

74
00:04:45.536 --> 00:04:48.159
When he realized they were lost, it was too late.

75
00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:52.184
Becky cried, and Tom did his best to comfort her.
